<title>USA: Williams Field Services to sell gas assets.</title>
<headline>Williams Field Services to sell gas assets.</headline>
<dateline>TULSA, Okla. 1996-09-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Williams Field Services Group said on Tuesday it would sell its natural gas gathering and processing assets in western Colorado and eastern Utah to Wildhorse Energy Partners, a joint venture between KN Energy Inc and Tom Brown Inc.</p>
<p>Terms of the deal were not disclosed but Williams said in a statement the transaction was expected to be completed on or before November 1.</p>
<p>Wildhorse would acquire roughly 955 miles of natural gas gathering lines, two processing plants, a carbon dioxide treatment plant and a dew-point control plant, Williams said.</p>
